WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.528
In the last years of the Western Jin, Zu Ti and Liu Kun were colleagues and lived in the same room.

00:00:06.878 --> 00:00:12.038
The two often talked deep into the night, both wanting to do their part for the country.

00:00:12.388 --> 00:00:20.188
One night the rooster crowed, and Zu Ti at once woke Liu Kun, saying the hours before dawn were a fine time to practise martial arts.

00:00:20.538 --> 00:00:25.002
Liu Kun rubbed his eyes, at once picked up his sword, and went out together with him.

00:00:25.352 --> 00:00:33.104
From that day on, whenever the rooster crowed at midnight, the two got up and practised swordsmanship in the courtyard.

00:00:33.454 --> 00:00:40.798
Rain or shine, they persisted every day without a break, and their martial skills grew higher and higher.

00:00:41.148 --> 00:00:45.132
When the neighbours heard the sound of the swords, they all admired the two men's perseverance.

00:00:45.482 --> 00:00:49.826
Many years later, both men had become great generals whose fame spread far and wide.

00:00:50.176 --> 00:00:55.336
They always remembered the days of their youth, when they rose to dance with their swords at the rooster's crow.

00:00:55.686 --> 00:01:01.470
People use 'rising to dance at the rooster's crow' to praise diligent, unremitting people like them.

